@@ -28,3 +28,12 @@ and returns the result as a new value: neither `target` nor `patch` is mutated o
 A `patch` that is not an object (an array, a string, `null`...) replaces the target; an object patch merges
 member by member, a `null` member removing that member from the target. It throws an `Error` when `target`
 or `patch` is not a JSON value (such as `undefined` or `NaN`).
+
+## Creating a JSON Patch
+
+`createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returns a JSON Patch (RFC 6902) that turns `from`
+into `to` when given to `applyPatch`. The patch holds only what changed: unchanged members and array items
+are left out, nested changes are addressed by their own path, and equal inputs give an empty patch. It uses
+`add`, `remove` and `replace` only; an array insertion or removal in the middle is a single operation when
+the rest of the array is unchanged. Neither input is mutated or shared with the patch. It throws an `Error`
+when `from` or `to` is not a JSON value (such as `undefined` or `NaN`).
